  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency grant in response to the flood disaster in the Central region of Viet NamEmergency grant in response to the flood disaster in the Central region of Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam has experienced disasters unprecedented in scale throughout 2025, marked by extreme typhoons and historic floods in terms of intensity, frequency, and geographic reach. This succession of extreme events has overwhelmed local response capacities, leaving urgent needs for shelter, food security, and recovery assistance, leading to notable humanitarian challenges and official requests for assistance from the government.This project addresses urgent humanitarian needs in Viet Nam&#x2019;s flood&#x2011;affected southern central provinces namely Dak Lak, Gia Lai, Khanh Hoa and Lam Dong by providing life&#x2011;saving non&#x2011;food items (NFIs) to 8,000 most vulnerable households (estimated 32,000 individuals) and equipping local first responders for essential search and rescue. Implemented by IOM in close coordination with national and provincial authorities, the intervention ensures timely, targeted relief that protects displaced families, restores dignity, and strengthens community resilience in line with national disaster management strategies and international humanitarian commitments.</narrative>
  </description>
